1
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:04,663
Red, orange, yellow…

2
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:08,484
In autumn, the leaves change color, then fall.

3
00:00:08,534 --> 00:00:10,777
But where did the green go?

4
00:00:11,568 --> 00:00:14,133
Noah compares: a green summer leaf,

5
00:00:14,183 --> 00:00:15,702
a yellow autumn leaf.

6
00:00:15,752 --> 00:00:17,346
Same tree, same shape…

7
00:00:17,396 --> 00:00:19,264
but no green left at all.

8
00:00:20,052 --> 00:00:21,566
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:24,082 --> 00:00:24,699
Mini mode!

10
00:00:24,749 --> 00:00:28,037
The leaf is full of a green coloring, chlorophyll,

11
00:00:28,087 --> 00:00:30,707
which catches sunlight to feed the tree.

12
00:00:30,757 --> 00:00:33,227
In summer, it hides the other colors.

13
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:35,190
Shorter days, cold:

14
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:39,074
the tree stops making chlorophyll and takes back its pieces.

15
00:00:39,124 --> 00:00:41,858
The green fades, and the yellow and orange,

16
00:00:41,908 --> 00:00:43,721
hidden since summer, appear!

17
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,215
And the red?

18
00:00:45,265 --> 00:00:46,235
That one is new:

19
00:00:46,285 --> 00:00:49,932
some trees make it just before letting go of their leaves.

20
00:00:49,982 --> 00:00:52,226
Then a layer of cells cuts the stem:

21
00:00:52,276 --> 00:00:53,233
the leaf falls.

22
00:00:54,059 --> 00:00:55,211
The tree doesn't die:

23
00:00:55,261 --> 00:00:58,818
it rests through winter and grows green leaves again in spring.

24
00:00:58,868 --> 00:01:00,871
Meanwhile, leaf piles are all ours!

25
00:01:01,662 --> 00:01:03,923
That's why leaves change color.

26
00:01:05,219 --> 00:01:08,371
The green disappears and reveals the hidden yellow;

27
00:01:08,421 --> 00:01:10,618
the red, though, is made in autumn.

28
00:01:11,459 --> 00:01:12,136
With an adult:

29
00:01:12,186 --> 00:01:15,515
collect leaves and line them up from the greenest to the reddest.

30
00:01:15,565 --> 00:01:17,384
Which one still has a little green?

31
00:01:18,918 --> 00:01:21,143
And how do fish breathe underwater?

32
00:01:21,193 --> 00:01:22,492
The answer tomorrow.
